From b1cf5b60e45a662b541d4013a08fbb86398506e9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Junction 2026 team <junction2026@localhost>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 17:21:42 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] feat(backend): capture state snapshots of a live runtime
 session

POST /api/projects/{project_id}/state_snapshots saves what the project's live
session holds right now to <storage>/state_snapshots/<project>/<YYYYmmdd-HHMMSS-mmm>/;
GET lists the saved snapshots, newest first.

- state.json: capture time (local, UTC, monotonic) and each source's sample
  time and age; project, session (control, dataset), environment; follower
  joint positions as the session measured them, and the leader's while it
  teleoperates (the command the follower is sent); servo ticks derived from
  the calibration; robot ids, names, types, serial numbers and a copy of
  their calibration; camera settings, and a RealSense's intrinsics, depth
  scale and alignment as its publisher recorded them; Studio version and git
  revision; and what could not be captured, and why.
- <camera>.color.png (lossless), and for a camera with depth
  <camera>.depth.png (uint16 millimetres, 0 = no depth) and
  <camera>.depth_preview.png (colorized over the camera's depth range).

It is read-only: it copies the session store's latest values like a
recording does, so it opens no device a second time, sends a robot nothing,
reads no robot bus and leaves a recording undisturbed. Without a live session
with an environment it answers 409 no_live_session.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
